## Decisions

- 2026-10-18: Nick: "Merge it and apply the SMLSC messages. Also apply the revert action." PR #112 merged (merge commit on main), release PR #110 merged → v1.21.0. Revert built on `feat/revert-member-confirmed-issue` as PR #113 (ISC-170..180). Shape mirrors PR #109's exit from `issued`: a real state-machine event (`REVERT_ISSUE`) rather than a raw status write, so `validEvents`, the admin button gating and the audit transition label all come for free. Eligibility is read from the audit trail (latest status_change to `issued` has `action: member_confirmed_receipt`) rather than a new column: the trail is already the only record of *how* a request was issued, and a column would need a migration and a backfill for nothing. Permission is `ISSUE` (same audience as the hand-over and the issuer email), not `APPROVE_EXEMPTION` like the payment demand. The member is emailed the admin's reason because the member made the original claim and would otherwise see their request silently go backwards; it honours the ready-for-pickup preference since that is the state they are back in. After a revert the flagged location still offers the form, so a genuine hand-over can be re-reported. Rejected: reverting admin-recorded issues through the same button (a real hand-over has its own correction paths and reverting it would strip the issuer attribution); a `collected: false` flag on ISSUE instead of a new event (would have to be threaded through every ISSUE branch).

- 2026-10-18: refined: QA + advisor round on PR #111 (expiry-update stage). QA (`accessbuddy-qa-verify`, independent run) returned NOT READY on two real findings: (1) `bun run typecheck` failed on the new test file, because my "typecheck clean" came from a background run started before the test existed; standing rule: the typecheck that counts is the one on the final tree, after the last file lands, with `--force` so turbo cannot serve a cached pass. (2) `ownedByThisMember` was computed for every row with a matching owner, so a member's own `deactivated` fob (always offered under "Previously Assigned" for the old stages) vanished from Programming/Pickup/Issued; fixed by gating the flag to the two statuses the extended query added (`expired`, `returned`). Low findings taken: tenant + owner predicates on the staging UPDATE, `previousDeactivatedAt` in the snapshot, unowned-active message. Advisor (closing call) raised cancel-programming not restoring the previous owner, lost/stolen fobs being re-enabled, a linked request being acted on at confirm, crons touching `expired` rows, and a past default expiry. Verified not applicable: confirm-programming never reads `requestId` (grep, now pinned by the confirm test keeping an ISSUED request), cron 1c / warnings / permission pass select ACTIVE only and auto-close needs a return request, `membershipYearExpiry` is always at least two months ahead, lost/damaged/stolen statuses are already ineligible. Taken: the free-text revoke reason is shown to the admin before staging and to the programmer in the dashboard line ("was deactivated: <reason>"), an "Update staged" tag on the member page, the default date in the expiry hint, and a notice stating the fob stays expired until confirm and what cancel does. Rejected: restoring the previous owner on cancel-programming (cancel is the programmer withdrawing the job, not a reversal of the admin's assertion that the member holds the fob; a generic route would need an audit-driven restore pa